\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project Specification: Local Project Hub \'97 Cross-Platform Desktop Application\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 1. Project Goal\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Transform the existing Local Project Hub into a polished, distributable desktop application for 
\f0\b macOS and Windows
\f1\b0 , preserving as much of the existing implementation as possible.\
Local Project Hub is a desktop control center for managing locally hosted Python projects. Users can register project folders, configure how each project starts, launch and stop processes, and access project dashboards from a shared application window.\
The finished application should feel like a normal desktop product rather than a Python script. Users should not need to install Python manually, open a terminal, or execute commands to install or update the Hub.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Primary objectives:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Preserve existing functionality and avoid unnecessary rewrites.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Support macOS and Windows with platform-appropriate application packages.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Provide a proper application icon, menus, version information, and installer.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Support user-initiated application updates from within the application.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Protect registered projects, configuration, logs, and other user data during installation and updates.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Make development and future releases straightforward.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Begin by Auditing the Existing Project\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Before changing the architecture, inspect the entire existing codebase and identify:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The current GUI framework and application entry point.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How the application starts, monitors, and stops project processes.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How project registrations, settings, and application state are stored.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How Python interpreters, virtual environments, dependencies, ports, and dashboard URLs are configured.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Any macOS-specific paths, commands, APIs, or assumptions.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Existing error handling, logging, and tests.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Which components can be reused without modification.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Produce a short architecture assessment listing what can be retained, what needs adaptation for Windows, and what genuinely needs replacement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Do not rewrite the application from scratch just to make it distributable.
\f1\b0  Prefer incremental changes and preserve the existing GUI framework if it is suitable for a cross-platform release. Recommend a framework migration only when there is a concrete technical reason.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Cross-Platform Compatibility\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The application must support macOS and Windows.\
Implement platform-specific behavior behind small, clearly defined interfaces where practical. Examples include:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Application data and configuration directories.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 File paths and filesystem permissions.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Starting, monitoring, terminating, and restarting subprocesses.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Discovering or selecting Python interpreters.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Opening dashboard URLs in the user's browser when needed.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Launch-at-login registration and removal.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Installer, application icon, and update mechanisms.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Use cross-platform Python libraries and APIs wherever possible. Avoid shell commands and hard-coded paths that work only on macOS.\
Do not assume that a Python project registered in the Hub is itself cross-platform. The Hub should clearly report when a project's interpreter, dependencies, startup command, or other requirements are unavailable on the current operating system.\
Keep platform-specific code isolated so that supporting additional platforms later does not require redesigning the core application.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. Desktop Application Experience\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The Hub must run in its own desktop application window.\
Provide:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A proper application name, icon, and version number.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Native or framework-appropriate application menus.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 An About dialog containing the installed version.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Clear startup, shutdown, and error states.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A settings area for application preferences.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A menu item such as 
\f0\b Help \uc0\u8594  Check for Updates
\f1\b0  or 
\f0\b About \uc0\u8594  Check for Updates
\f1\b0 , following platform conventions.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Clear feedback when an update is available, downloading, installing, or failing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Preserve the existing project-management interface and workflows wherever possible. Do not redesign the entire interface unless necessary.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 5. In-App Updates \'97 A Core Requirement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Users must be able to update Local Project Hub without manually downloading a new release, opening a terminal, or running installation commands.\
Implement a reliable update mechanism appropriate for the chosen desktop framework and packaging strategy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Required user experience\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The user opens the application's menu and selects 
\f0\b Check for Updates
\f1\b0 .\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The application checks a trusted release endpoint for a newer compatible version.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If no update exists, it reports that the application is up to date.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If an update exists, it displays the new version and a concise summary of the release notes.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The user selects 
\f0\b Download and Install
\f1\b0 .\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The application downloads the appropriate update for the user's operating system and CPU architecture, verifies its integrity and authenticity, and prepares the installation.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If the application must restart, it asks the user to restart now or finish later when safe.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The application restarts into the new version and confirms the result.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The update process must not require administrator privileges unless the chosen installation location or a specific operation genuinely requires them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Update implementation requirements\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Use a maintained update mechanism compatible with the selected application framework.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prefer a secure, established update system over a custom implementation that executes arbitrary downloaded scripts.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Publish versioned releases and platform-specific update artifacts through a reliable release channel, such as GitHub Releases or an equivalent hosting service.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Verify downloaded artifacts using the updater's supported signature verification or cryptographic integrity mechanisms. Do not rely on HTTPS alone as proof that an artifact is the authentic publisher release.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Support separate macOS and Windows artifacts, including the appropriate CPU architectures.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Handle network failures, interrupted downloads, invalid signatures, incompatible releases, and insufficient disk space gracefully.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Never replace a running executable in an unsafe manner. Use the framework's supported update-and-restart procedure.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If an update fails, preserve the existing installation wherever possible and provide actionable error information.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Display meaningful release notes and version numbers.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Allow the user to decline or defer an update.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Do not claim an update succeeded until the installed version has been verified.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 An optional background check may notify the user when a new version is available, but the user must retain control over installation and restart timing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 6. Application Packaging and Installation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Create distributable release packages for both operating systems.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 macOS\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Produce a proper 
\f2\fs26 .app
\f1\fs24  bundle and, where appropriate, a distributable 
\f2\fs26 .dmg
\f1\fs24  installer.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Include the application icon, metadata, and required runtime components.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Configure code signing and Apple notarization for normal distribution outside the development environment.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ensure the updater can install future versions correctly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Windows\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Produce a conventional installer, such as an 
\f2\fs26 .exe
\f1\fs24  installer or 
\f2\fs26 .msi
\f1\fs24  package, using a format compatible with the selected updater.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Include the application icon, required runtime components, and version metadata.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Support normal installation and uninstallation.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sign release artifacts where feasible to establish publisher identity and improve user trust.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ensure the application and updater work without requiring users to install Python separately.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The initial release must not require users to clone a repository, install development tools, configure an environment manually, or run a terminal command.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 7. Protect User Projects and Data\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Application updates must be independent of registered projects.\
Maintain a strict separation between:\
