\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 12. Implementation Strategy\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Work in small, reviewable phases rather than attempting a complete rewrite in one pass.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Phase 1 \'97 Audit:
\f1\b0  Understand the current implementation and establish a baseline of working features.\

\f0\b Phase 2 \'97 Compatibility:
\f1\b0  Resolve Windows incompatibilities and separate platform-specific operations.\

\f0\b Phase 3 \'97 Packaging:
\f1\b0  Produce a working, installable build for each operating system while preserving the current interface.\

\f0\b Phase 4 \'97 Updating:
\f1\b0  Implement the in-app update workflow, including version checks, safe installation, restart behavior, and failure recovery.\

\f0\b Phase 5 \'97 Polish:
\f1\b0  Add icons, menus, About/version information, and optional launch-at-login settings.\

\f0\b Phase 6 \'97 Release:
\f1\b0  Configure signing, distribution, CI builds, and clean-machine testing.\
At the end of each phase, report the changes made, tests performed, remaining issues, and the next recommended step. Do not mark a phase complete based solely on code inspection when it requires a real installation or runtime test.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Final Guiding Principle\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Build a dependable desktop application around the existing Local Project Hub, not a new application that merely resembles it.\
Prioritize preserving working code, protecting user data, predictable process management, safe in-app updates, and easy installation on both macOS and Windows. Choose the simplest architecture that meets these requirements and explain any proposed major framework change before implementing it.\
